/*
 * gvcp.c - GigE Vision control server (gvcp.h), stage 2 of
 * docs/protocol/GEV_PROTOCOL_DESIGN.md.
 *
 * GigE Vision 2.2: packets ch. 15-16, control channel privilege and heartbeat ch. 10,
 * bootstrap registers ch. 27. The manufacturer map (0xA000..) is generated by
 * tools/gev/gev_features.py into gev_regs.h and docs/protocol/gev/REGISTER_MAP.md;
 * the same script makes the GenApi XML (gev_xml.c) served by READMEM at FirstURL.
 * Bit masks below are C masks; the standard numbers bit 0 = the MSB.
 *
 * Manufacturer writes go through vmsp_call(): the VMSP control opcode that does the same
 * (0x0112, 0x0120, 0x0130..0x0134, 0x0140, 0x0142, 0x0145, 0x0150, 0x0160..0x016A,
 * 0x0302) with its checks and locks. Reads come from the getters those handlers use,
 * or from the 0x0300 / 0x0122 answers. One task owns all state here (no locks).
 *
 * Not yet (stage 3 and later): GVSP streaming (stream channel registers are stored
 * only), events (message channel registers stored only), PACKETRESEND (accepted and
 * ignored, not advertised), DHCP / link-local address.
 */

